  ▶ $ cd /home/runner/work/yoyo-evolve/yoyo-evolve && gh issue cre… (5 lines) ✓ (1.4s)

I've committed the fix as 3148a8f8, titled "Fixes #1129". yoyo review now refuses a mistyped flag with exit 2 and a did-you-mean, instead of treating it as a file path or a PR number. Build, the full cargo test run, clippy with -D warnings and fmt --check all pass.

Output from the built binary, run in an empty /tmp directory with </dev/null:
```
$ yoyo review --quik
error: unknown flag '--quik' (did you mean --quick?) for `yoyo review`. Nothing ran.   (exit 2)
$ yoyo review --thorogh
error: unknown flag '--thorogh' (did you mean --thorough?) for `yoyo review`. Nothing ran.   (exit 2)
$ yoyo review --print
error: unknown flag '--print' for `yoyo review`. Nothing ran.   (exit 2)
$ yoyo review -- --weird-file
  error: file not found: --weird-file   (exit 1)
```

What changed:
• `src/verb_flags.rs`: review now has its own flag list, and a new review_arg builds the review target from argv. --pr N, --prN and --pr=N all work; --pr=N used to fail as "invalid PR number: =N".
• `src/commands_git_review.rs`: the old starts_with("--pr") check is replaced by is_pr_arg, so --print and --pretty are no longer read as PR numbers.
• `src/dispatch_sub.rs`: the review handler checks flags before anything else runs, and its argument-building function now just calls review_arg.
• Beyond the task's spec: --provider, --model, --api-key and --base-url are accepted after review. The review code already read them, but they also ended up in the file path, so yoyo review --model m src/x.rs said "file not found: --model m src/x.rs". They are now left out of the path. Without this change they would have been refused as unknown flags.
• REPL `/review`: it doesn't go through the shell flag check, so it gets no refusal. Two things change there: /review --print now says "file not found" instead of "invalid PR number: int", and /review --pr=5 now works.

Tests:
• Unit tables in verb_flags.rs cover the refusal message for each bad input and check that every previously accepted form still produces the same review target.
• is_pr_arg has its own unit test.
• Two tests in tests/unknown_flag_refusal.rs run the real binary and check the exact error text and exit code. Their normal-input rows (bare review, --quick, --thorough, a missing file, the --pr forms, -- --weird-file) all exit 1 at the same review error as before.
• As a sanity check, I deleted the review entry from the flag list, which turned all four new tests red. I restored it in the same command and confirmed it was restored.

Housekeeping: dispatch_sub.rs shrank from 2640 to 2637 lines, and I updated its entry in tests/module_size.rs. The non-interactive review section of docs/src/usage/commands.md now lists the flags and the -- escape.

Not fixed: yoyo review -- --quick still reviews at quick effort instead of looking for a file named --quick. The flags and path are still passed to the review code as one joined string, which gets split on spaces again. This predates the change. Because this commit closes #1129, I filed it as #1130, including the shape of the fix.
